---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const points = [
  { icon: 'cloud-off', t: 'No server', d: 'Your phone connects straight to your Mac. We do not run a relay, and we could not see your traffic if we wanted to.' },
  { icon: 'lock', t: 'No account', d: 'There is nothing to sign up for, so there is no profile, email address or password to protect.' },
  { icon: 'shield', t: 'Encrypted end to end', d: 'After pairing, every message is encrypted with keys held only by your phone and your Mac.' },
  { icon: 'sparkles', t: 'AI stays on the Mac', d: 'Ask, Smart Clipboard and Organize Tiles use Apple Intelligence on your own Mac.' },
];
---
<Base title="Privacy" description={`How ${site.name} handles your data: no server, no account, end-to-end encryption and on-device intelligence.`}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow reveal">Privacy</span>
      <h1 class="display reveal">The short version:<br /><span class="grad">we never see it.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">{site.name} was built so that your living room stays yours. This page explains exactly what the apps do with your data, in plain language.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap points">
    {points.map((p, i) => (
      <div class="card reveal" style={`--d:${i * 70}ms`}>
        <span><Icon name={p.icon} size={22} /></span>
        <h2 class="h3">{p.t}</h2>
        <p class="muted">{p.d}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <article class="wrap prose">
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
      <p>Your tiles, their artwork, your scenes and the list of paired remotes are stored in your Mac's Application Support folder. They are not uploaded anywhere. Removing the app's data removes all of it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>How the phone and the Mac talk</h2>
      <p>The remote finds your Mac with Bonjour on your local network, or over Bluetooth LE, and then opens a direct connection to it. Nothing is routed through the internet.</p>
      <p>The first time a phone connects, the Mac shows a 6-digit code. The code is mixed into the key exchange, so a device that does not know it cannot complete pairing. From then on, messages are encrypted with ChaCha20-Poly1305 using keys agreed with X25519. Each side keeps its own long-term key, and you can remove any paired remote in Settings.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>When the Mac uses the internet</h2>
      <p>{site.name} itself only goes online to fetch pictures for tiles: the icon and poster of a site you add as a link, and site icons shown in the app switcher. Those requests go straight from your Mac to that site and are cached locally.</p>
      <p>While <b>Show What's New</b> is on (Settings → Top Shelf), the Mac also fetches public show listings and pictures from TVmaze, and Apple's public music and movie charts, once a day. The requests are the same for every Mac in your region, whatever is on your Home screen: they carry no account, no list of your apps and nothing about what you watch. A music tile's shelf shows what that app is playing on your Mac, which needs no request at all. Turn Show What's New off and none of these requests are made.</p>
      <p>Opening a tile opens that app or website, which then follows its own privacy policy, as it would if you had opened it yourself.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Local Network and Bluetooth</b>, on both devices: so the phone and the Mac can find each other.</li>
        <li><b>Accessibility</b>, on the Mac: to deliver the keyboard, trackpad and media keys you press on your phone, and to move windows.</li>
        <li><b>Photos</b>, on the Mac, only if you choose an album for the screensaver: to show it. Photos never leave your Mac; your phone sees only the album's name.</li>
        <li><b>Automation</b>, on the Mac, asked once per browser: to switch to a tab that is already open instead of opening a duplicate. Private windows are skipped.</li>
        <li><b>Microphone and Speech Recognition</b>, on the phone: only while you hold the mic button. Speech is turned into text by your phone's built-in recognition, under Apple's or Google's terms.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>Apple Intelligence</h2>
      <p>Ask, scene drafts, Organize Tiles and Smart Clipboard run on your Mac using Apple Intelligence. What you say or paste is not sent to us or to a third-party AI service. If Apple Intelligence is off or unavailable, these features hide themselves and the rest of the app works as before.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>Diagnostics reports</h2>
      <p>When you ask for help, {site.name} can copy a diagnostics report: versions, settings, permission states, counts and the current session's log, with names, titles, links and addresses left out. It goes to your clipboard and nowhere else. You decide whether to paste it into an email.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>Analytics and tracking</h2>
      <p>The apps contain no analytics, advertising or tracking code.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reveal">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .points { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .points .card { padding: 26px; }
  .points span { width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 13px; display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--accent); background: rgba(126, 168, 255, 0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(126, 168, 255, 0.2); margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .points p { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 0.94rem; }
  @media (max-width: 980px) { .points { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .points { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .prose { max-width: 760px; margin-top: clamp(64px, 9vw, 110px); display: grid; gap: 48px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.55rem; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .prose p, .prose li { color: #c3c7d3; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .prose p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .prose ul { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .prose li { padding-left: 22px; position: relative; }
  .prose li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 2px; top: 0.72em; width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); }
  .prose b { color: #fff; font-weight: 620; }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
